hello my name is dr whitney holden and i  have a phd in microbiology and  immunology i teach biology and research  at asmsa  because of my background as a researcher  i'm always looking for new innovations  to test in my classroom  i use technologies like quizlet live  paradigm a variety of podcasts  hhmi biointeractive and more in the past  five years i've used four different  learning management systems and five  different approaches to labs for remote  students at various schools i work with  including filming my own virtual labs  for them to share online resources with  other educators i serve on merlot's  international biology editorial board  where i help to curate the life science  oer collection  i also teach an independent research  capstone course this class is about so  much more than just competing in science  fair i develop well-rounded  scientifically literate students by  focusing on statistical analysis and  peer-reviewed scientific literature  i'm even working with my most recent  isaf finalists to submit their research  for publication to international student  journals i also co-direct  two major outreach programs the first is  advanced biology plus  where i provide curriculum and training  to dozens of arkansas ap biology  classrooms  participating schools have gone from  only 10 percent of their students  passing the ap biology exam to 40  percent of their students passing that  exam  the second program is the arkansas  summer research institute which is for  underrepresented students in stem  they learn technical skills like  electrophoresis and cad and 3d printing  while also focusing on essential  professional skills things like resumes  entrepreneurship networking and more i  even run a youtube channel called  biology professor with 40  000 subscribers and almost 4  million views from virtually every  country in the world through my work i  have found  the keys to building truly innovative  experiences  are mentorship teamwork respect  and a willingness to challenge myself as  well as my students  thank you
 

